%S A398711 0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,5,153,5815,218097,9348400,478632938
%N A398711 Number of unlabeled n-element posets whose linear-extension-majority digraph contains a simple directed cycle.
%C A398711 For a finite poset P, let E(P) be the set of linear extensions of P, equipped with the uniform distribution. The linear-extension-majority (LEM) digraph D(P) has vertex set P and a directed edge x -> y whenever Pr(x precedes y in a random linear extension) > 1/2. Comparable pairs are included: if x < y in P then x -> y. a(n) counts isomorphism classes of n-element posets for which D(P) contains at least one simple directed cycle.
%C A398711 a(n) = 0 for n <= 8, and a(9) = 5, are due to Gehrlein and Fishburn, who searched exhaustively through n = 9. Terms a(10)..a(13) are the "All" column of Table 2 of De Loof, De Baets, and De Meyer; a(14) is from the exhaustive order-14 census in Gupta (2026).
%C A398711 One poset may carry simple cycles of several lengths, so a(n) is not the sum of the counts by cycle length. The definition uses the full LEM relation, including comparable pairs, matching Gehrlein and Fishburn (1990) and De Loof, De Baets, and De Meyer (2010). Through n = 14 the counts agree with those obtained from the incomparable-pairs-only subdigraph, but that agreement is computational, not a theorem for all n. No formula or recurrence is known.
%H A398711 K. De Loof, B. De Baets, and H. De Meyer, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.camwa.2009.12.021">Counting linear extension majority cycles in partially ordered sets on up to 13 elements</a>, Comput. Math. Appl. 59 (2010), 1541-1547.
%H A398711 W. V. Gehrlein and P. C. Fishburn, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/0898-1221(90)90239-G">Linear extension majority cycles for small (n <= 9) partial orders</a>, Comput. Math. Appl. 20 (1990), 41-44.
%H A398711 Anish Gupta, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.23926">Balance Constants, Majority Cycles, and the Gold Partition Conjecture through Fourteen Elements</a>, arXiv:2607.23926 [math.CO], 2026.
%H A398711 Anish Gupta, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21696940">Release 2 archive</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A398711 Anish Gupta, <a href="https://github.com/agupta/gold-partition-conjecture/releases/tag/v2.0.0">Source release v2.0.0</a>, GitHub, 2026.
%e A398711 a(n) = 0 for 0 <= n <= 8: no poset on at most 8 elements has a simple LEM cycle (Gehrlein and Fishburn).
%e A398711 a(9) = 5: exactly five isomorphism classes of 9-element posets have a simple directed cycle in D(P) (Gehrlein and Fishburn). Each such cycle has length 3, since the n = 9 row of Table 2 of De Loof et al. is 5 in the length-3 column and 0 in every longer column; the census in Gupta (2026) confirms no longer cycle occurs at n = 9.
%Y A398711 Cf. A000112.
